98K ranks in the above the sector median among Consumer Cyclical peers. Each employee generates $14K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $589 per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 7\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity).","financial_summary":["Bob's Discount Furniture, Inc. is a mid-cap consumer cyclical business with a $2.7B market cap on $2.4B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +4% over the past three years, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 10% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically, with gross margins sitting at 46%.","The business throws off $81M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 3 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.35\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 4.5\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and interest coverage of 20\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Management returns a meaningful 15.9% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 3.6% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Very elevated short interest (28.2% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Carries a 43% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.4337608838123772},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Heavy insider selling (net $138.9M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-138882565.75},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Consumer demand is fundamentally cyclical \u2014 a recession compresses both unit volume and pricing power, and operating leverage cuts both ways.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"E-commerce margin compression and tariff exposure \u2014 digital competition erodes pricing power while trade policy reshuffles supply-chain cost structures overnight.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Returns on capital have been remarkably steady for 5 years \u2014 durability is the real test of a moat","Piotroski score 7/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Bob's Discount Furniture (BOBS) Released Third Quarter Results, Is It Still Below Fair Value?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/retail/nyse-bobs/bobs-discount-furniture/news/bobs-discount-furniture-bobs-released-third-quarter-results","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794385457.008,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.904,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Bob's Discount Furniture (NYSE:BOBS) Q3 2026","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/retail/bobs-discount-furniture-nysebobs-q3-2026","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794323520.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.832,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Bob\u2019s Discount Furniture (NYSE:BOBS) Price Target Raised to $25.00","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/09/bobs-